Instructs RPM to enforce package signature verification on the target.

Only packages signed by a signature known to RPM are allowed to be
installed. Otherwise the installation will be blocked and an error will
be generated.

To use this template, add the following to your setup line:

    --templates feature/rpm-required-sig

Add the following lines to conf/local.conf:

    INHERIT += "sign_rpm"
    RPM_GPG_PASSPHRASE = "foo"
    RPM_GPG_NAME = "bar"

Additionally, you can set %_pkgverify_level rpm macro to "signature" or
"all" on the target to enhance the package verification level (see the
/usr/lib/rpm/macros file for details).

#@TYPE: Wrtemplate
#@NAME: rpm-required-sig
#@DESCRIPTION: Instructs RPM to enforce package signature verification on the target.
